# DURABLE REPRO — calling a `Callable`-typed STRUCT FIELD (`h.f(...)`) is
# lowered as a USER METHOD CALL on the struct, not as an indirect call through
# the field, so the program fails to LINK.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend):
#   `gg check` -> "OK: no semantic errors"
#   `gg build` -> /usr/bin/ld: undefined reference to `Holder__f'
# The emitted C declares and calls a static method symbol that no one defines:
#   void Holder__f(void*, void*);
#   Holder__f(__v5, __v6);
# — note the TWO parameters: a `self` pointer plus the argument, which is the
# method-call ABI. `h.f` was never read as a field.
#
# ⚠ THE PARSE IS THE ROOT, NOT THE ABI: `h.f(&a)` parses as a MethodCall rather
# than an `Expr::Call` whose callee is a field access, so the whole indirect-call
# family (`__callable_N` / `__gorget_closure_call_N` dispatch, and every
# argument-ownership check that hangs off it) is bypassed. The safety pass sees
# a method call with no resolvable `DefId` and checks nothing.
#
# ⚠ SECOND, SEPARABLE DEFECT VISIBLE IN THE SAME SHAPE: the field's declared
# function type is not checked against what is stored in it. Declaring the field
# `Callable[void(int)]` (a BARE `int` parameter) and initialising it with
# `bump`, whose signature is `void(&int)`, is accepted silently — while the
# identical mismatch at a LOCAL binding is correctly rejected:
#     Callable[void(int)] f = bump
#     -> error[E_TypeMismatch]: expected `void(int)`, found `void(&int)`
# This fixture declares the field with the MATCHING `void(&int)` type so that
# the link failure is isolated; the mismatch cell is recorded here, not asserted.
#
# SCOPE — one cell: a `Callable` field on a plain struct, called with a `&`
# argument, on the C backend. Not sampled here: the LLVM lane, a bare argument,
# a field reached through a nested path, or a `Callable` field on an enum
# payload.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): `h.f(&a)` calls the stored callable indirectly and
# writes through the `&` argument, so the program prints `11`.
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE CANNOT RUN UNTIL FIXED: the link step produces no binary.
#
# The seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so no const-fold can elide the call.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (the `Callable` indirect-call costume census).
struct Holder:
    Callable[void(&int)] f

int seed():
    return 10

void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(bump)
    int a = seed()
    h.f(&a)
    print(a)
